{
  "id": "LLOG.2.5.multi_justif_scale",
  "category": "logical",
  "scenario": "Multi-justification at scale: one keyed logical fact Blk{X} is justified once per In input whose Have is absent (the build scheduler's block_input mechanism). As each Have arrives the matching justification is withdrawn; with all 34 present Blk must retract fully. A TMS dependency table that withdraws an activation by leaving a tombstone its probe stops at makes a colliding later activation unreachable, and that withdrawal is dropped, leaving Blk's justif_count above 0. Scale-sensitive (TMS hash collisions), so it needs many justifiers: 68 facts are left (34 In + 34 Have, no Blk), and one orphaned Blk makes 69.",
  "rules_ds": "schema In scope logical:\n    id: Int key\nschema Have scope logical:\n    id: Int key\nschema Blk scope logical:\n    k: String key\nrule block:\n    In i\n    no Have h where h.id == i.id\n->\n    emit Blk logical k: \"X\"\n",
